{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 ICMP redirect acceptance on node1 for current and future interfaces.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor installed all/default/wildcard settings at 0, verified every current interface at 0, rebooted the node, and confirmed the file and live values remained effective afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7b7f4fc25593471c","cmd-3f8590495f3f4f47","cmd-8bbc8c334e494ad8","cmd-121d2b2f37de4afc","cmd-31c1661bbb5b4f9f","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Persistently disable IPv4 source-routed packet acceptance on node1 for current and future interfaces.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persistent policy explicitly covers all/default/wildcard interface scopes. All current interfaces reported 0 before and after a confirmed reboot, demonstrating persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-957ea05364d3469d","cmd-3f8590495f3f4f47","cmd-8bbc8c334e494ad8","cmd-121d2b2f37de4afc","cmd-31c1661bbb5b4f9f","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so none remained or required reversion. The only state-changing actions were installing and applying the task-specific sysctl policy and performing the mandatory reboot. Temporary-file handling was bounded, package health remained intact, and the failed SSH service existed both before and after execution. Temporary-file and socket differences are consistent with normal reboot turnover.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a162c45ee8f46d5","cmd-8bbc8c334e494ad8","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both required IPv4 hardening outcomes are satisfied. The restart protocol captured the original boot identity, task-relevant healthy state, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity, and recovered sysctl service, policy, addressing, and routing. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["Whole-system health was not clean: cmd-f08ac7feea7a408e reported a degraded system state, while lifecycle snapshots show the same pre-existing failed ssh.service before and after execution. Task-relevant sysctl and network recovery were directly demonstrated, but globally healthy service state was not."]}
